l"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shafer</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Biraro</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamali</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> . <source>HIV prevalence and incidence are no longer falling in Uganda&#x02014;a case for renewed prevention efforts: evidence from a rural population cohort 1989&#x02013;2005, and from ANC surveillance</source>. <comment>XVI International AIDS Conference.</comment> <comment>13&#x02013;18 August, Toronto.</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b28"><label>28</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mishra</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrere</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group>  <article-title>Evaluation of bias in HIV seroprevalence estimates from national household surveys.</article-title> <source>Sex Transm Infect</source> <year>2008</year>;<volume>84</volume><issue>Suppl I</issue>:<fpage>i63</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>i70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18647869</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>